Optional Qore TypeScript catalogue
==================================

Activate explicitly for a Qore process with:

 export QORE_TYPESCRIPT_MASTER_ACTION_SCRIPT=/usr/share/qore-v8-app-catalogue/dist/index.js

Then load TypeScriptActionInterface or use Qore's data-provider tools. The package
includes production JavaScript dependencies, not Jest or development tools.
Service credentials are provided separately by the application. Installed files
are immutable; application indexes and caches belong in application-owned paths.

This local prototype has not been cleared for public redistribution. See
schema-provenance.json and the dependency notices for outstanding provenance.

HubSpot schemas
---------------

The package contains no HubSpot OpenAPI documents. After reviewing HubSpot's
Developer Terms (https://legal.hubspot.com/hs-developer-terms), run as the account
that will run the application:

 qore-hubspot-schemas update
 qore-hubspot-schemas run -- YOUR_APPLICATION [arguments]

The catalogue environment variable above is still required. This explicit command
fetches current documents for the supported v3 APIs (OpenAPI 3.0 format), not an
arbitrary new API generation labelled LATEST. Forms currently requires HubSpot's
v3 preview entry. The public catalogue endpoint may change or disappear; it has
no availability guarantee. No schema download occurs at build time, during dpkg
installation, on application startup, or from a maintainer script.

The updater checks all ten documents, local references, API server URLs and the
66 supported operations. It applies known Deals/Lists path aliases and retains
all 78 declared HubSpot action identities, then materializes those actions using
the installed Qore runtime. It activates the snapshot only if every check passes.
This checks schema compatibility; it does not test authenticated service calls.

The default cache is $XDG_CACHE_HOME/qore/hubspot, or ~/.cache/qore/hubspot.
Use --cache-dir /absolute/path before the command for a service-owned cache.
Do not run the updater as root for a service using another account. Each snapshot
has its own SHA-256 directory and manifest with source locations and input/output
hashes. Keep the snapshot directory private to the account; do not edit it.
The run wrapper selects a verified snapshot and passes its immutable path through
QORE_HUBSPOT_SCHEMA_SNAPSHOT. Existing processes keep their selected snapshot;
restart them explicitly after an update. A service manager can instead set that
variable to the absolute path printed by qore-hubspot-schemas status. Do not point
it at a mutable symlink. No active snapshot is silently selected at module import.

Without a valid pinned snapshot, HubSpot retains its complete discovery inventory
and reports HUBSPOT-SCHEMAS-UNAVAILABLE when initialized. Other apps remain usable.
An incompatible update fails without changing the active snapshot:

 qore-hubspot-schemas status
 qore-hubspot-schemas rollback
 qore-hubspot-schemas rollback SNAPSHOT_SHA256

Rollback rechecks compatibility with the currently installed catalogue and Qore.
Snapshots from an older contract may require a fresh download after an upgrade.
To work offline, obtain authorized v3 documents on a connected machine and copy
companies.swagger.json, contacts.swagger.json, custom-objects.swagger.json,
deals.swagger.json, forms.swagger.json, leads.swagger.json, lists.swagger.json,
products.swagger.json, tickets.swagger.json and users.swagger.json into one
private directory, then run:

 qore-hubspot-schemas import /absolute/path/to/documents

Update/import/rollback use an exclusive .update-lock containing the writer PID.
After a crashed updater, confirm that PID is no longer running before removing
only the stale lock. Old snapshots are retained for running processes and rollback;
remove an obsolete snapshot manually only after those processes have stopped.
Deleting or purging the package does not delete application-owned caches. Manage
retention and removal according to your applicable HubSpot terms and requirements.
